   "evidence": "Surgery.lean:78 `surgerySlope := ((h.neighborhood i).preferredFramedBoundaryTorus h\u2081 h\u2082).slopeEquiv.symm (r i)`; SeifertFraming.lean:36-38 'Replacing the longitude by `\u03bb - n \u00b7 \u03bc` gives the preferred framing'.",
   "file": "TauCeti/LowDimTopology/SolidTorusNeighborhood/Orientation.lean",
   "fix": "Say that coefficients are read in the preferred framing (`TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.preferredFramedBoundaryTorus`), and add that the reflection sends \u03bc to \u2212\u03bc and n to \u2212n, so it fixes \u03bb\u2080 and still turns r into \u2212r.",
   "issue": "The module docstring says surgery coefficients are read in \u03a6's framing (`FramedBoundaryTorus.value`, \u03bb = \u03a6(1, exp(2\u03c0it))) and argues the sign flip from 'reverses \u03bc, keeps \u03bb'. But `surgerySlope`, used by `IsWeeksManifold`, reads values in the preferred framing with longitude \u03bb\u2080 = \u03bb \u2212 n\u00b7\u03bc, so the stated argument does not cover the coefficients the definition actually uses.",
   "line": 17
  }
 ],
